      "id": "6dcdfa9c-1460-40bb-a531-c64366c2f1aa",
      "name": "Extract Page Text",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.html",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1168,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Job posting:\n\n{{ ($json.postingText || \"\").slice(0, 20000) }}\n\nCandidate CV:\n\n{{ ($('Get Saved CV').first().json.cv_text || \"NO CV PROVIDED\").slice(0, 15000) }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are a Job Posting Extractor. Turn a long job posting into a summary readable in under 30 seconds. Use ONLY information in the posting; never add requirements, tools, or tasks that are not there.\n\nFields:\n- isJobPosting: false if the text is not a job posting (then leave other fields as empty strings / empty array).\n- jobTitle: the title as written in the posting.\n- pay: copy figures exactly as stated, keeping currency and period (hourly, monthly, annual), e.g. \"$65,000 - $80,000 per year\". Include bonus, commission, or equity only if mentioned. If only implied (e.g. \"competitive salary\") write \"Not stated (described as competitive)\". If absent write \"Not stated\". Never estimate or guess.\n- toolsSkills, education, experience, other: brief keywords, a few words per item, comma-separated, not sentences (\"SQL\", not \"strong proficiency in writing complex SQL queries\"). Include soft skills only if the posting stresses them; skip generic ones like \"team player\" or \"detail-oriented\". If the posting separates required from preferred, add \"(preferred)\" after preferred items. If a category is not mentioned write \"Not stated\". \"other\" covers certifications, languages, licenses, clearances, work authorization; use an empty string if none.\n- keyTasks: 4 to 8 bullets, each starting with a verb (Build, Analyze, Maintain, Present, Coordinate), one short line of about 15 words or fewer. Merge duplicates and combine closely related duties. Skip company boilerplate, mission statements, benefits, and \"other duties as assigned\".\n- note: if the posting is vague or contradictory (e.g. two different pay ranges), one short note; otherwise an empty string.\n\n- fitVerdict: compare the candidate CV against the posting's requirements and tasks. \"Fit\" = meets the core requirements; \"Partial fit\" = meets some core requirements with notable gaps; \"Miss\" = lacks most core requirements. If the CV says NO CV PROVIDED, use \"No CV\" and leave fitMatches and fitGaps empty.\n- fitMatches: 2 to 5 short keyword items from the CV that match the posting's requirements.\n- fitGaps: up to 5 short keyword items the posting requires that the CV does not show; empty if none.\nBase the comparison only on what the CV and posting actually say.\n\nThe input may be a scraped web page containing navigation and unrelated text; focus on the main job posting."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "id": "0b5be9e4-466a-4ffb-9dda-c964d6925120",
      "name": "Summarize Job Posting",
